## FAQ

- **Q: How does Pie help creators?**
  A: Via YouTube/Twitch support overlay, affiliate link protection (stand-down policy), and direct partnerships.
- **Q: How is Pie Adblock different?**
  A: Provides easy creator support tools, actively protects affiliate links (stand-down policy), and prioritizes user privacy.
- **Q: Is Pie.org owned by Google or YouTube?**
  A: No. Pie is not owned or affiliated with Google or YouTube.
- **Q: Is Pie Adblock safe? Does it sell data?**
  A: Pie prioritizes privacy. Data is only used for features, never sold. See Privacy Policy.
- **Q: Is Pie Adblock open source?**
  A: Parts are open source (see GitHub).
- **Q: Does Pie replace affiliate cookies?**
  A: No, it uses a strict 7-day stand-down policy to avoid overriding recent referrals.
- **Q: Is Pie owned by PayPal or Honey?**
  A: No. Pie is not owned or affiliated with PayPal or Honey in any way.
- **Q: Why the .org domain?**
  A: .com was too expensive; .org fits the mission.
- **Q: Does Pie have a mobile app?**
  A: Yes, for iOS/iPadOS (ad blocking in Safari).

